      "name": "acquisition_driver",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "How the expense was generated (automated vs manual vs standard procurement) can drive both the classification as travel-related and the likelihood of decline (automated entries may face different validation). A common cause plausibly surfaced from data."
    },
    {
      "name": "travel_expense_indicator",
      "causal_role": "treatment",
      "named_in_query": true,
      "rationale": "This is the candidate cause -- being a travel expense -- whose effect on decline the query explicitly asks about ('travel expenses get declined')."
    },
    {
      "name": "department_origin",
      "causal_role": "confounder",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Department both influences the volume/type of travel spending (treatment exposure) and the decline rate (budget policies differ by department). A genuine common cause surfaced from data, though it duplicates an existing original column."
    },
    {
      "name": "source_id_presence",
      "causal_role": "other",
      "named_in_query": false,
      "rationale": "Whether a source_id is populated is a record-provenance/data-quality flag. It is more plausibly a consequence of the entry channel or a collider on completeness than a common cause of both travel-status and decline; weak as a confounder."
    }
  ],
  "treatment_present": true,
