  ],
  "confounder_quality": 0.5,
  "rationale": "The set does supply an explicit treatment (travel_expense_indicator) matching the query's causal focus, and several confounders (acquisition_driver, department_origin, asset_category) were surfaced from data rather than named in the query and are plausible common causes of both travel-status and decline. This is partial evidence of genuine causal reasoning. However, quality is only moderate: source_id_presence is a provenance/data-quality flag rather than a true common cause, department_origin merely re-labels an existing column, and none of the confounders are strongly justified via described mechanisms. No mediators are mislabelled, but the confounding structure is loosely motivated."
}
